Cache __index chain lookups for metatable classes.

Carts that build classes from metatables (an instance whose metatable is
its class, each class falling back to its parent through __index) read
inherited fields, methods and missing names by walking the chain: two
hash lookups per level.  luaV_gettable now asks a 128-entry cache keyed
by the key's text and the receiver's metatable first.  An entry records
the tables the result depended on and is valid while none of them has
been written, given a new key, resized or had its metatable set (bit 7 of
'flags', cleared by all of those); a hit then looks the key up in the
final table only.

The cache replaces fastchain from z8lua-index-chain.patch, which probed up
to four __index levels for _ENV names before every slow lookup; removing
its calls also shrinks the BRAM-resident VM loop.  luaV_gettable, the hit
path and chainrefill are outside BRAM.

